findings.body:
The `apiUrl` option was dropped from the `scheduling.init` call. `post-scheduling/index.js` reads `options.apiUrl` directly, and `scheduling.init()` passes its undefined argument straight through. The read `options.apiUrl` then throws a TypeError, which rejects the `Promise.all` in `initServices` and stops Ghost from starting.

The PR description says nothing about this change, and nothing else in the diff needs it. Restore the original call.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="365-370"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The original call passed `apiUrl: urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)`. That is the only input `PostScheduler` uses to build callback URLs, and its constructor throws `IncorrectUsageError` when it is missing.

::suggestion{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="368-370"}
scheduling.init({
    apiUrl: urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)
}),

`slack.listen()` was removed from the `Promise.all` batch. That call is the only place `server/services/slack.js` registers its `post.published` and `slack.test` listeners, so Slack notifications for newly published posts stop working and the Slack test ping no longer responds.

The PR description covers only Pingomatic, so this looks like an accidental deletion. The `slack` require at line 319 is also left unused.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="361-366"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Nothing in the diff replaces the registration. Ghost's Slack integration will go silent with no error.

In the base commit, `emailAddressService.init()` was awaited on its own before `Promise.all`, with a comment saying the newsletter and email services depend on it. This PR moves it into the same `Promise.all` as those services. `emailService.init()`, `emailAnalytics.init()`, and `members.init()` can now start before the email-address service has finished initializing.

The PR is only meant to remove xmlrpc, so this ordering change looks unintended. The comment above the batch is now orphaned from the code it describes.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="349-352"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The base code ran `await emailAddressService.init()` as a separate step before the batch, so every dependent service had it ready. The new code gives no such guarantee.

After this change, `slack` (line 319) and `urlUtils` (line 343) are declared in `initServices` but never used. `urlUtils` was only used by the `scheduling.init` argument, and `slack` only by the `slack.listen()` call. This is the classic removed-call-leaves-import pattern. Ghost's lint config flags unused variables, so CI lint will fail.

If `scheduling.init` is restored as recommended above, `urlUtils` becomes used again and only `slack` needs to go, or `slack.listen()` should be restored and both stay used.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="343-343"}
